cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  variant-fm-benchmark: calibration and fusion of splice and sequence-based
  variant-effect predictors benchmarked against saturation genome editing
  functional assays
message: >-
  If you use this software or the derived data, please cite both the software
  (this file) and the accompanying paper listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Ningyi
    affiliation: Department of Biological Sciences, National University of Singapore
    email: cliffzhang@u.nus.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3020-4044"
repository-code: "https://github.com/oneone00-11/variant-fm-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark of splice and sequence-based variant-effect predictors against
  saturation genome editing (SGE/MAVE) functional assays in seven
  hereditary-cancer genes (BRCA1, BRCA2, BARD1, PALB2, RAD51C, VHL, BAP1),
  with elastic-net fusion, leave-one-gene-out isotonic/Platt calibration,
  ACMG evidence-strength translation, and external validation on the held-out
  gene TP53.
keywords:
  - variant effect prediction
  - saturation genome editing
  - splice prediction
  - calibration
  - ACMG evidence strength
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
